  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For the five-vertex tree T* with edge set {ca, cb, cd, de}, using ordinary (not induced) subgraph comparability on every induced five-vertex subset exactly as frozen in source.md and problem.md, f(T*) = 8. Specifically, 2 K_4 is T*-exact, no nine-vertex T*-exact graph exists, and heredity excludes all larger orders.",
